{
 "cases": [
  {
   "i": 14130,
   "title": "Notifications failing due to upstream dependency timeouts in US-West",
   "description": "We are observing a high rate of delivery failures for transactional notifications sent via the Session Controller in the US-West production environment. The logs indicate that the request is timing out before reaching the notification service, with error messages pointing to an upstream dependency failure. The notification itself is never delivered to the end user. No user impact has been reported yet, but we need to understand why the controller is hanging on these upstream calls."
  },
  {
   "i": 14131,
   "title": "Mobile app is slow and failing intermittently",
   "description": "The analytics dashboard seems to be causing issues with the mobile app. It's really slow and sometimes just doesn't load. We are seeing this in staging but it's hard to pin down when it happens. No specific errors showing up on the frontend, just hanging."
  },
  {
   "i": 14132,
   "title": "Severe latency and query timeouts on Analytics Dashboard (Sandbox)",
   "description": "Our sandbox environment in the APAC region is experiencing significant delays when accessing the Analytics Dashboard. Complex queries are timing out after approximately 30 seconds, and simple load times are upwards of 10 seconds. This is impacting about 223 developers who are currently blocked from testing new features. We need assistance optimizing the backend query performance or increasing the timeout thresholds for this environment."
  },
  {
   "i": 14133,
   "title": "Incorrect tax calculations leading to failed renewals and chargebacks",
   "description": "We are seeing a critical issue in production (ANZ) where subscription renewals are failing. The initial invoice generation appears to be calculating the tax amount incorrectly. Because the total charged does not match what the customer expected, several banks are flagging these as unauthorized, resulting in chargeback notices. It's unclear if the Invoice Service is generating the wrong numbers or if the renewal logic is failing to process the correct amounts properly. Approximately 739 users are affected by these billing errors."
  },
  {
   "i": 14134,
   "title": "Audit log gaps and retention policy enforcement failure",
   "description": "In the US-East production environment, we have identified a discrepancy between our configured retention policies and the actual audit logs available in the Analytics Dashboard. Several entries that should have been archived or deleted based on the 90-day retention rule are still present, while conversely, some critical security events from earlier this week seem to be missing entirely. This affects a small subset of admin accounts (3 users) but poses a compliance risk. We need to verify why the retention job isn't applying correctly to these specific log streams."
  },
  {
   "i": 14135,
   "title": "Webhooks not firing from Analytics Dashboard",
   "description": "We have configured several webhooks in the Analytics Dashboard to trigger actions in our internal systems when specific metrics thresholds are crossed. Since yesterday, none of these webhooks have fired, despite the conditions being met and the events being visible in the UI. We have checked our receiving endpoint and it is online and accepting requests. The issue seems to be that the Dashboard itself is not initiating the outbound webhook calls. One user reported this behavior."
  },
  {
   "i": 14136,
   "title": "Login issues in Dev environment",
   "description": "Can't log into the SSO module. Getting 401 errors. A few people in the dev team are blocked. We haven't changed anything recently."
  },
  {
   "i": 14137,
   "title": "Unexpected session expirations causing account lockouts",
   "description": "A small group of users (6 accounts) in the US-West production environment are reporting that they are being logged out prematurely. Upon trying to re-authenticate immediately, their accounts are temporarily locked out due to failed login attempts, even though they are entering the correct credentials. The Session Controller appears to be dropping the valid session tokens after a very short duration, which conflicts with our configured idle timeout of 30 minutes. We need to investigate why these specific sessions are invalidating early and triggering the security lockout protocol."
  },
  {
   "i": 14138,
   "title": "Data mismatch in Cohort Builder export vs UI",
   "description": "We are noticing a discrepancy in the Cohort Builder tool within the production ME region. When we view a cohort in the UI, the user count is significantly different from the number of records returned when we export that same cohort definition. For example, a cohort showing 12,000 users in the interface exports as 11,850 rows. This affects approximately 56 users who rely on these exports for campaign targeting. The filters applied are identical in both the UI query and the export request, so we are unsure why the data sets are diverging."
  },
  {
   "i": 14139,
   "title": "Feature flags not applying correctly in Staging",
   "description": "We have enabled several new feature flags in the Analytics Dashboard for our staging environment in ANZ, but they are not appearing for the target user groups (119 users). It is unclear whether the issue lies within the Dashboard's configuration layer not propagating the flags correctly, or if the underlying audit/log tracking system is failing to register the user attributes required for the flag targeting logic. The expected behavior is that these users should see the new UI elements, but they are seeing the legacy view. We need to determine if the flag injection is happening or if the user identity resolution is failing."
  },
  {
   "i": 14140,
   "title": "High latency on Analytics Dashboard and mobile app in Staging",
   "description": "The staging environment in LATAM is performing poorly. We are seeing response times on the Analytics Dashboard exceed 15 seconds for most requests. Simultaneously, the companion mobile app, which pulls data from the same backend, is experiencing similar slowdowns and occasional freezes. This is impacting about 37 testers. We need to check if there is a resource bottleneck in the staging cluster causing both the web dashboard and the mobile API endpoints to degrade."
  },
  {
   "i": 14141,
   "title": "Critical Payment Gateway 429 Errors and Missing Webhooks",
   "description": "We are experiencing a critical outage in the staging EU-Central environment for Payment Gateway v2. We are receiving HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) errors for almost all transaction attempts, suggesting the gateway itself is rate-limiting us despite low traffic volume. Additionally, confirmation webhooks are not being sent to our endpoints after successful or failed transactions. This is blocking 21,361 simulated users from completing flows. We believe the gateway service is overloaded or misconfigured regarding its internal rate limits and event dispatching."
  },
  {
   "i": 14142,
   "title": "Password reset links expiring immediately in MFA Manager",
   "description": "Users in the EU-West production environment are unable to complete password resets because the links provided are expiring instantly. When a user clicks the reset link sent via email, they are redirected to an error page stating the token is invalid or expired. This is affecting 2,891 users who are currently locked out or need to update credentials. The MFA Manager seems to be generating these reset tokens with an extremely short TTL or failing to validate them correctly upon return."
  },
  {
   "i": 14143,
   "title": "Certificate warnings in Staging",
   "description": "Getting security warnings about expired certificates when trying to connect to the session service. Not sure if it's impacting everyone or just some clients. It started recently."
  },
  {
   "i": 14144,
   "title": "Refunds not reflecting in customer accounts",
   "description": "We have processed several refunds via the Payment Gateway v2 in the ME production region, but the funds are not appearing in the customers' accounts. The transaction status shows 'success' in our internal logs. It's unclear if the issue is with the gateway's processing of the refund instruction or if the subsequent update to the customer's balance via the API interface is failing to commit. 14 users are currently experiencing this delay. We need to verify if the refund transaction is being correctly relayed and acknowledged by the downstream balance update service."
  }
 ]
}
